# Secrets — MUST stay ahead of any `git init` in this directory.
# agents/create-campaign-v2/.env.development currently holds a live DB password
# in plaintext. See portal/project-plan/BACKLOG.md B-11 for the rotation plan.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
secrets.json
credentials.json

# All Claude Code tooling/config, root- and portal-level (per-user request 2026-08-24) — not
# part of the deployable application. Note: this also drops portal/.claude/settings.json (the
# team-wide, conservative allow-list) and the implement-task/review-task skills from what gets
# pushed — fine for "just get Render building the app", worth knowing if anyone else picks this
# repo up later and wonders why those skills aren't there.
.claude/

# Not part of the deployable application — working/reference material, not code Render needs
# to build or run the portal. (gitignore has no inline "# comment" syntax — a trailing comment
# on the same line as a pattern becomes part of the pattern itself, so each note is its own line.)

# The separate create-campaign agent services — also holds a real (throwaway) DB password in
# agents/create-campaign-v2/.env.development.
agents/

project-plan/

database/
# Repo orientation doc for AI agents/developers — not read by any build step (confirmed: only
# referenced in code comments in portal/back-end/Dockerfile and portal/docker-compose.yml,
# pointing a human reader at it, never COPYed or parsed). Also somewhat tailored to this local
# machine (nvm paths, a macOS Keychain lookup command) rather than portable across clones.
CLAUDE.md

# The capabilities deck, business user guide, and this deploy guide.
portal/architect-review/

# Generated task-progress / architecture dashboards.
portal/project-plan/index.html
portal/project-plan/architecture.html

*.pdf

# Dependencies and build output.
# coverage* (not just coverage/) — this repo's back-end has many run-specific report dirs
# (coverage-e2e, coverage-crypto, coverage-t047-all, ...) that a bare `coverage/` rule misses,
# since gitignore does no partial/prefix matching without an explicit wildcard.
node_modules/
dist/
build/
coverage*/
.next/
.turbo/

# Local tooling
.DS_Store
*.log
npm-debug.log*
.idea/
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json

# Test artefacts
playwright-report/
test-results/
*.lcov
